cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "EviSSL: Evidential Semi-Supervised Skin Lesion Segmentation"
abstract: >-
  Semi-supervised segmentation methods select which unlabelled pixels to learn
  from using a confidence threshold, which cannot distinguish a pixel the model
  knows nothing about from a pixel whose evidence genuinely conflicts. This work
  replaces the threshold with a subjective-logic decomposition of an evidential
  (Dirichlet) head: vacuity gates the per-pixel consistency weight and
  dissonance tempers the sharpening temperature. The method is trained on a
  0.96M-parameter depthwise-separable U-Net with a gated axial bottleneck, 32
  times smaller than the reference 31M-parameter U-Net, and is evaluated with
  overlap, boundary-distance, calibration and uncertainty-ranking metrics under
  paired statistical tests.
